# Regular differentials of the level N function field as F(τ) dτ

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_mdifferentiable`
(`fc27f9fc-c074-52b0-905f-212471904b97`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `a7c4745a-d7a4-5a51-80f0-a56599741478`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $A_N =$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the algebra of
functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by `jAnalytic` together with all Fricke functions
`fricke N v` for $0 \neq v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$. Let $K$ be a field which is simultaneously a
$\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_N$-algebra, compatibly, and which is a fraction field of $A_N$. Write
$\Omega_{\mathrm{reg}} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials ℂ
K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials.html#L26) for the $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of
$\Omega_{K/\mathbb{C}}$ of those $\omega$ such that for every place $v$ of $K/\mathbb{C}$ — that is,
every valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $K$, and a
principal ideal ring — there is $f$ in that valuation subring with $\omega = f \cdot d(t_v)$, $t_v$
a uniformiser of $v$. Two assertions are made. First, every $\omega \in \Omega_{\mathrm{reg}}$ has
the shape $\omega = (a/b)\cdot d(c/e)$ for functions $a,b,c,e : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ lying in
$A_N$ with $b \neq 0$ and $e \neq 0$, where $a,b,c,e$ are mapped into $K$ by the structure map and
$d$ is the universal derivation of $K$ over $\mathbb{C}$. Second, there is an injective
$\mathbb{C}$-linear map $\Psi : \Omega_{\mathrm{reg}} \to (\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C})$ such that
each $\Psi\omega$ is holomorphic on $\mathbb{H}$, and such that for every $\omega$ and every
presentation $\omega = (a/b)\cdot d(c/e)$ as above (with $a,b,c,e \in A_N$, $b,e \neq 0$) one has,
for all $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$, $$\Psi\omega(\tau)\, b(\tau)\, e(\tau)^2 = a(\tau)\bigl(e(\tau)\,
c'(\tau) - c(\tau)\, e'(\tau)\bigr),$$ the derivatives being complex derivatives of $c$ and $e$
transported to $\mathbb{C}$ along `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`.

This is the analytic half of the classical identification of the differentials of the first kind on
the modular curve of level $N$ with holomorphic differentials $F(\tau)\,d\tau$ on the upper half
plane: a regular differential of the function field $K$ is determined by, and determines, a
holomorphic function $F$ on $\mathbb{H}$ through $\omega = F(\tau)\,d\tau$, the correspondence being
recorded by the displayed cross-multiplied identity so as to avoid dividing by the zeros of $b$ and
$e$. It is used by
[`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective),
where the image of $\Psi$ is matched with weight $2$ cusp forms of level $N$.

